# DAX Measures

All measures are stored in the `Measure` table and use the `Students` table.


## Summary

| Measure | Purpose | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Total Students | Count of students | 1,000 |
| Average Final Score | Mean final exam score | 83.5 |
| Pass Rate | Share of students not graded F | 98.8% |
| At Risk % | Share with grade D or F | 10.1% |
| Top Performers % | Share with grade A | 28.4% |

## Measures

### Total Students
```DAX
Total Students = COUNTROWS ( Students )
```

### Average Final Score
```DAX
Average Final Score = AVERAGE ( Students[FinalScore] )
```

### Pass Rate
```DAX
Pass Rate =
DIVIDE (
    CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( Students ), Students[FinalGrade] <> "F" ),
    [Total Students]
)
```

### At Risk %
```DAX
At Risk % =
DIVIDE (
    CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( Students ), Students[FinalGrade] IN { "D", "F" } ),
    [Total Students]
)
```

### Top Performers %
```DAX
Top Performers % =
DIVIDE (
    CALCULATE ( COUNTROWS ( Students ), Students[FinalGrade] = "A" ),
    [Total Students]
)
```

## Validation

| Check | Calculation | Matches dashboard |
|---|---|---|
| At risk | (89 + 12) / 1,000 = 10.1% | ✅ |
| Top performers | 284 / 1,000 = 28.4% | ✅ |
| Pass rate | (1,000 − 12) / 1,000 = 98.8% | ✅ |

## Notes

- `DIVIDE` is used instead of `/` to avoid divide-by-zero errors.
- Measures respond to the Gender and Internet Access slicers through filter context.
